 "notes": {
  "images": "Female_FaceFront 457x824, Female_FaceSide 510x772 (profile facing left), Female_Back 542x851, Female_Front 1024x1536",
  "conventions": "Same as the Male tables in project_reference.py: *_l = the character's left (image right in the front view). eye_*, eye_l_in/out, eye_r_in/out and side 'eye' are reference-only iris centres / opening corners; the TPS pins the eyes from eye_openings and ignores names that model_face_points does not define.",
  "hairline_head_top": "hairline and head_top are placed where the MODEL's points land on the drawing (hairline = eye_z + 0.034 m = mid-forehead, head_top = skull top under the hair), not at the drawn hair edge, so the brow band is not squeezed 4-5x. The drawn hairline is at front (228, 196) / side (64, 166); the hair silhouette top is at front y=13 (bun) / side y=62 (hairline_drawn / head_top_drawn, reference only). If model_face_points' hairline is ever moved to the real scalp edge, use hairline_drawn.",
  "scale": "front ~2360 px/m (ear rim to ear rim 416 px = 2*(ear_x+0.011)), side ~2050 px/m (eye to chin).",
  "strip": "hair = main mass above/behind the face + ribbons for the loose strands beside the face, the ears and the neck. The ears are left out of the polygons. beard is empty (kept so layer_masks finds the key).",
  "blackout": "Female_Back: a stray strand of hair from the next sheet cell at the left edge (x 0-11, y 78-136) is painted black before anything else.",
  "auto_strip_margin": "On the face drawings the automatic dark-mass strip only counts masses within this many px of the strip polygons: without it the dense hatching under the chin (FaceFront) was taken for a hair mass and filled with a skin disc. The ears in FaceFront are stripped whole (hair crosses them; the profile draws the ears), and FaceSide's black top at the bottom is stripped so no dark mass sits next to the neck.",
  "soften": "Regions whose dark hatching is turned into a soft warm shadow (strip_hair): the dense hatch under the lower lip projected as a black smear on the chin. FaceSide: the ear hollow (its black fill projected as a blot in the ear).",
  "hair_polygons": "The FaceFront/FaceSide hair polygons' lower edges follow the drawn hairline (forehead and temples); the first version sat 10-25 px inside the hair and its edge line survived on the forehead."
